      "title": "MinGW-w64: Fix extcap build output path",
      "message": "MinGW-w64: Fix extcap build output path\n\nBuild output must not be placed in run/<config>/subdir.\n\nThis should be done using CMAKE_GENERATOR_IS_MULTI_CONFIG instead of just\nMSVC but that wasn't working for me when I tried briefly.\n",
      "author_name": "João Valverde",
      "author_email": "j@v6e.pt",
      "authored_date": "2021-07-16T15:30:11.000+01:00",
      "committer_name": "Wireshark GitLab Utility",
      "committer_email": "gerald+gitlab-utility@wireshark.org",
      "committed_date": "2021-09-22T16:34:37.000+00:00",
      "trailers": {},
      "extended_trailers": {},
      "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/commit/3adfca384be8e485f96a96d7bf7064ef0c225f32"
    },
    {
      "id": "fa525649bea7ee6ec14958e123b386755d0518ac",
      "short_id": "fa525649",
      "created_at": "2021-09-22T16:34:37.000+00:00",
      "parent_ids": [
        "9bce34ca67d1f057c2fcb910c030d2a160c69ade"
      ],
      "title": "CMake: Try to set a required try_run() definition in a more idiomatic way",
      "message": "CMake: Try to set a required try_run() definition in a more idiomatic way\n\nThis is applicable to every test (if we had more), not just HAVE_C99_VSNPRINTF.\n\nCould also be a #define but let's go with this for now. This takes\nadvantage of the stack based design of CMakePushCheckState.\n",
      "author_name": "João Valverde",
      "author_email": "j@v6e.pt",
      "authored_date": "2021-09-22T15:57:43.000+01:00",
      "committer_name": "Wireshark GitLab Utility",
      "committer_email": "gerald+gitlab-utility@wireshark.org",
      "committed_date": "2021-09-22T16:34:37.000+00:00",
